// A split block's tile (fw its format word; after ``rows``: its R rows of each slot in yt), st[S_GN] its place j in
// its group's tiles (gate then up; a block holds whole groups): part 0 or 1 (gate, up), rows o .. of the part's 64 (k of
// them valid). A gate tile's rows go into the slot's window (gw [slot][64] fp32, rows o ..: per 16 rows of the window
// the lanes of [0 x 16 | y | 0 x 16] in gs that fall on them); an up tile's rows times act(bf16(gate)) of the window's
// rows o .. into the tile's rows 0 .. k - 1 (the group's outputs o ..), the window cleared after the group's last.
// Sets the next tile's place and, in this block, its format. Returns the outputs to stage: k, or 0.
__attribute__((noinline)) int {{ p }}_gusplit(int32_t *__restrict ws, int S, int R, int fw)
{
